IMPORT prelude

-- Therapeutic Goods Regulations 1990 (Cth), as they meet a patient: a person given, prescribed, compounded, imported or
-- trialled a medicine or biological, who has been harmed by it or wants to know whether it reached them lawfully and
-- with the information they were owed.
--
-- SEAT: the patient. Every exported question is phrased as that person would ask it: "Must my medicine come with a
-- consumer medicine information leaflet?", "Could I lawfully be given an unapproved medicine because my life was at
-- risk?", "Was the statement about me sent to the regulator in time?", "Can an authorised prescriber's authority cover
-- me?", "Can I import this medicine for my own treatment?", "Was the trial I took part in run within the conditions?".
-- The Regulations give the patient no right to sue. They decide whether the medicine was lawfully in the patient's hands
-- (the Register exemptions, the special-access and authorised-prescriber conditions, the clinical-trial conditions), what
-- the patient had to be told (the consumer medicine information), and what consent the life-threatening exemption needs.
-- Those are facts a claim under other law (negligence, the Australian Consumer Law) builds on.
--
-- Where the Regulations hand a matter to a judgment ("seriously ill", "reasonably likely", "good medical practice",
-- "sufficient information", "clearly legible", "otherwise serious"), the answer is conditional on it, asked as a fact.
-- Borrowed instruments (the Poisons Standard, the Customs Act 1901 and Customs (Prohibited Imports) Regulations 1956, the
-- TGA templates, the Good Clinical Practice guideline, the National Statement) are asked as facts.
--
-- Provisions covered: reg 2 ("immediate family", "medicinal cannabis products"), regs 9A, 9B, 12(1)-(3) with Schedule 5
-- items 1 and 6 and Schedule 5A item 3, 12A, 12AB(2), 12AD, 12B(1), (1A), (1B) and (1C) (the tables asked as one fact),
-- (2), (5), (6), 12BA(1)-(3), 12BB, 12C(1)-(3), (5), Schedule 10 Part 1, Schedules 12 and 13. The Acts Interpretation Act
-- 1901 s 36(1) item 6 and s 36(2) (Saturdays and Sundays only), applied to regulations by the Legislation Act 2003
-- s 13(1)(a), for the 28 days in reg 12A(3).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 131 (register id F2026C01012), compilation date 5 October 2026, includes amendments up to
-- F2026L01167, deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/F1996B00406.txt (retrieved 6 November 2026). Today's text is
-- applied to every date (NOTES.md). Penalties are in penalty units; the value of a penalty unit is not used.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Therapeutic Goods Regulations 1990 (Cth), from the seat of the patient`

§§ `Dates and periods`

-- Built-in date functions only (no daydate), so nothing here collides with a library's YMD.
GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` `d` `m` `y` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY `d` `m` `y`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`day number of` `the day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is on or after` `a` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `a` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is before` `a` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `a` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `days after` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

-- 1 January 1990 was a Monday; days 5 and 6 of each week counted from it are Saturday and Sunday.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`falls on a Saturday or Sunday` `the day` MEANS
    ((DATE_SERIAL `the day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL (`the date` 1 1 1990)) MODULO 7) AT LEAST 5

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(2), applied by Legislation Act 2003 s 13(1)(a): if "the last day for doing the
-- thing is a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday ... the thing may be done on the next day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday
-- or a holiday". Public holidays (s 36(3)) are not counted: they depend on the place (NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`moved off a weekend` `the day` MEANS
    IF `falls on a Saturday or Sunday` `the day`
    THEN `moved off a weekend` (1 `days after` `the day`)
    ELSE `the day`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(1) item 6: a period "expressed to begin after a specified day ... does not include
-- that day" (Example 6). So the last day of "within N days after" a day is that day plus N, moved off a weekend.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of` `n` `days after` `the day` MEANS `moved off a weekend` (`n` `days after` `the day`)

§§ `The duty with a deadline, as a regulative rule`

DECLARE `Statement party` IS ONE OF
    `the person who completed the statement`

DECLARE `Statement act` IS ONE OF
    `send a copy of the statement to the Secretary`

-- reg 12A(3): "A person who completes a statement referred to in subparagraph (2)(a)(iii) in relation to a medicine or
-- biological that is given to a person must send a copy of the statement to the Secretary within 28 days after the
-- medicine or biological is given to the person." Penalty: 10 penalty units; (3A) strict liability. The timeline is in
-- day numbers and the rule starts on the day the medicine was given.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Statement party` `Statement act`
`reg 12A(3) -- the person who completed the statement must send a copy to the Secretary within 28 days after the medicine is given` MEANS
    PARTY `the person who completed the statement`
    MUST  `send a copy of the statement to the Secretary`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the person who completed the statement` BECAUSE "reg 12A(3): an offence of strict liability (reg 12A(3A)), 10 penalty units"

DECLARE `Done in time or not` IS ONE OF
    `there is no such duty on these facts`
    `done in time`
    `not done in time`
    `still open until` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

-- Not a provision of the Regulations: the helper that runs the rule over what happened. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an
-- EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED, and OTHERWISE takes a breach and a rule still waiting alike. Where the act has been done,
-- FULFILLED means in time; where it has not, the helper asks whether doing it today would still keep the rule.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Statement party` `Statement act`
      `the start` IS A DATE
      `the act has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the act was done` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Done in time or not`
`the outcome of` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` (`day number of` `the start`) (LIST (WAITUNTIL (`day number of` `the day the act was done`)), (EVENT `the person who completed the statement` `send a copy of the statement to the Secretary` (`day number of` `the day the act was done`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` (`day number of` `the start`) (LIST (WAITUNTIL (`day number of` `today`)), (EVENT `the person who completed the statement` `send a copy of the statement to the Secretary` (`day number of` `today`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open until` `the last day`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

§§ `Definitions`

-- reg 2: "immediate family of a person means: (a) a spouse, de facto partner, child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or
-- sibling of the person; or (b) a child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling of a spouse or de facto partner of
-- the person." A closed "means" definition.
DECLARE `Whose treatment` IS ONE OF
    `my own`
    `my spouse or de facto partner`
    `my child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling`
    `a child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling of my spouse or de facto partner`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `whose` IS A `Whose treatment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is my immediate family` `whose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `whose`
    WHEN `my spouse or de facto partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `my child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling of my spouse or de facto partner` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Schedule 5 item 1: "the importer or the importer's immediate family".
GIVEN `whose` IS A `Whose treatment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is for me or my immediate family` `whose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `whose`
    WHEN `my own` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `is my immediate family` `whose`

-- reg 9B(4), (5): "human embryo means a live embryo that has a human genome or an altered human genome and that has been
-- developing for less than 8 weeks since the appearance of 2 pro-nuclei or the initiation of its development by other
-- means"; "any period when the development of the embryo is suspended is to be disregarded". 8 weeks is 56 days.
GIVEN `it is live` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has a human or altered human genome` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days since 2 pro-nuclei appeared or development began` IS A NUMBER
      `days its development was suspended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a human embryo` MEANS
        `it is live`
    AND `it has a human or altered human genome`
    AND (`days since 2 pro-nuclei appeared or development began` MINUS `days its development was suspended`) LESS THAN 56

-- reg 12A(5): "Category A patient means a person who is seriously ill with a condition from which death is reasonably
-- likely to occur within a matter of months, or from which premature death is reasonably likely to occur in the absence
-- of early treatment." Each limb is a clinical judgment, asked.
GIVEN `I am seriously ill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `death is reasonably likely within a matter of months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `premature death is reasonably likely without early treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a Category A patient` MEANS
        `I am seriously ill`
    AND (   `death is reasonably likely within a matter of months`
         OR `premature death is reasonably likely without early treatment`)

-- reg 12A(5): "informed consent, in relation to treatment or proposed treatment, means consent freely given by a person
-- on the basis of information concerning the potential risks and benefits of the treatment that was sufficient
-- information to allow the person to make an informed decision whether to consent to the treatment."
GIVEN `consent was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was freely given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was told the potential risks and benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what I was told was enough to make an informed decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is informed consent` MEANS
        `consent was given`
    AND `it was freely given`
    AND `I was told the potential risks and benefits`
    AND `what I was told was enough to make an informed decision`

-- Schedule 10 Part 1: item 1, "therapeutic goods (except therapeutic goods mentioned in another Part of this Schedule),
-- that: (a) contain a substance mentioned in Schedule 4, 8 or 9 to the Poisons Standard; or (b) ... meets the criteria
-- for mention in any of those Schedules"; items 2-15, a medical gas, a vaccine, an allergen (except for skin patch
-- testing on unbroken skin), a biotechnology medicine, an immunoglobulin, a radio contrast agent (except barium sulphate
-- preparation for radiological use), a radiopharmaceutical, a dialysis solution (except a haemodialysis solution), a
-- special dosage form, an injectable medicine dosage form, a blood product, goods referred to the Prescription Medicines
-- Authorisation Branch for evaluation as a prescription medicine, an excipient in goods in Part 1. Items 2-15 are asked
-- as one fact. The item 1 exception is asked as a fact (NOTES.md finding 2).
GIVEN `it contains or qualifies for a Poisons Standard Schedule 4, 8 or 9 substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in Part 2 or 3 of Schedule 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is one of the goods in items 2 to 15` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is in Part 1 of Schedule 10` MEANS
        (    `it contains or qualifies for a Poisons Standard Schedule 4, 8 or 9 substance`
         AND (NOT `it is in Part 2 or 3 of Schedule 10`))
    OR `it is one of the goods in items 2 to 15`

§ `The information that must come with my medicine` -- regs 9A, 9B, Schedules 10, 12 and 13

DECLARE `CMI answer` IS ONE OF
    `a document meeting Schedule 12 must come with it`
    `a document meeting Schedule 13 must come with it`
    `regulation 9A requires no document for it`

-- reg 9A(1): the sponsor of goods specified in Part 1 of Schedule 10 "and are included in the Register must not supply
-- the goods if the sponsor does not supply with the goods written information ... that meets the requirements for a
-- consumer medicine information document set out in Schedule 12". (1AA): "It is a defence ... if the goods are specified
-- in Schedule 3 to the Poisons Standard." (1A): the sponsor of goods "(a) specified in Schedule 3 of the Poisons
-- Standard; and (b) approved for registration on or after 4 July 1995; and (c) included in the Register" must not supply
-- them without a document meeting Schedule 13. (2): the information goes "(a) in the primary pack ... or (b) in another
-- manner that will enable the information to be given to a person to whom the goods are administered or otherwise
-- dispensed".
@export Must my medicine come with a consumer medicine information leaflet, and which kind (reg 9A)?
GIVEN `it is on the Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the medicine included in the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods (it has an AUST R or AUST L number)?
      `it contains or qualifies for a Poisons Standard Schedule 4, 8 or 9 substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain a substance in Schedule 4 (prescription only), 8 (controlled drug) or 9 of the Poisons Standard, or one that meets the criteria for those Schedules?
      `it is in Part 2 or 3 of Schedule 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a complementary medicine, antiseptic, sunscreen or other non-prescription good that the TGA accepted does not meet the criteria for Poisons Standard Schedules 4, 8 or 9 (Schedule 10 Part 2 or 3)? Answer no if unsure.
      `it is one of the goods in items 2 to 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a medical gas, a vaccine, an allergen (not for skin patch testing), a biotechnology medicine, an immunoglobulin, a radio contrast agent (not barium sulphate), a radiopharmaceutical, a dialysis solution (not haemodialysis), a special dosage form such as a patch or osmotic pump, an injectable, a blood product, or a prescription medicine referred for evaluation?
      `it is a Poisons Standard Schedule 3 medicine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a Schedule 3 (pharmacist only) medicine under the Poisons Standard?
      `the day it was approved for registration` IS A DATE @desc The day it was approved for registration, ISO 8601 (it matters only for a Schedule 3 medicine; any date otherwise)
GIVETH A `CMI answer`
DECIDE `Must my medicine come with a consumer medicine information document` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`it is on the Register`)
           THEN `regulation 9A requires no document for it`
           IF `it is a Poisons Standard Schedule 3 medicine`
              AND `is on or after` `the day it was approved for registration` (`the date` 4 7 1995)
           THEN `a document meeting Schedule 13 must come with it`
           IF `it is a Poisons Standard Schedule 3 medicine`
           THEN `regulation 9A requires no document for it`
           IF `is in Part 1 of Schedule 10` `it contains or qualifies for a Poisons Standard Schedule 4, 8 or 9 substance` `it is in Part 2 or 3 of Schedule 10` `it is one of the goods in items 2 to 15`
           THEN `a document meeting Schedule 12 must come with it`
           OTHERWISE `regulation 9A requires no document for it`

-- reg 9A(1), (1A): "Penalty: 10 penalty units" each; strict liability for the Schedule element ((1AAA), (1B)). A zero
-- means the offence's physical elements are not made out on these facts.
@export What fine can the sponsor face for supplying my medicine without the consumer medicine information it needed (reg 9A)?
GIVEN `it is on the Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the medicine included in the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods?
      `it contains or qualifies for a Poisons Standard Schedule 4, 8 or 9 substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain a Poisons Standard Schedule 4, 8 or 9 substance, or one that meets the criteria for those Schedules?
      `it is in Part 2 or 3 of Schedule 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a complementary or other non-prescription good the TGA accepted does not meet the criteria for Schedules 4, 8 or 9? Answer no if unsure.
      `it is one of the goods in items 2 to 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a medical gas, vaccine, allergen, biotechnology medicine, immunoglobulin, radio contrast agent, radiopharmaceutical, dialysis solution, special dosage form, injectable, blood product, or prescription medicine referred for evaluation?
      `it is a Poisons Standard Schedule 3 medicine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a Schedule 3 (pharmacist only) medicine?
      `the day it was approved for registration` IS A DATE @desc The day it was approved for registration, ISO 8601 (any date if not Schedule 3)
      `the sponsor supplied a compliant document with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the sponsor supply, in the pack or in another way that lets it be given to you, a leaflet meeting the requirements?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What fine can the sponsor face for supplying my medicine without the document` IS
    IF `the sponsor supplied a compliant document with it`
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `Must my medicine come with a consumer medicine information document` `it is on the Register` `it contains or qualifies for a Poisons Standard Schedule 4, 8 or 9 substance` `it is in Part 2 or 3 of Schedule 10` `it is one of the goods in items 2 to 15` `it is a Poisons Standard Schedule 3 medicine` `the day it was approved for registration`
         WHEN `regulation 9A requires no document for it` THEN 0
         OTHERWISE 10

-- Schedule 12 (and, word for word apart from the template's name, Schedule 13): clause 1, the document must "(a) be
-- written in English; and (b) be clearly legible; and (c) be written in language that will easily be understood by
-- patients; and (d) be consistent with product information". Clause 2: if it is "enclosed within, on a surface of, or
-- affixed to a surface of, the packaging", it must set out all the information the TGA template requires, in any order.
-- Clause 3: if not, it must set out that information "in the same order as the Template" and, "if it is supplied in
-- electronic form, it must be in the form of a PDF file or an HTML file".
@export Does the consumer medicine information leaflet I was given meet the requirements (Schedules 12 and 13)?
GIVEN `it is in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the leaflet written in English?
      `it is clearly legible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it clearly legible?
      `it is easily understood by patients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it written in language patients will easily understand?
      `it is consistent with the product information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it consistent with the medicine's product information (the document for health professionals)?
      `it came in or on the pack` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it enclosed in the pack, printed on it or attached to it?
      `it sets out everything the TGA template requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out all the information the TGA Consumer Medicine Information template requires?
      `it follows the template's order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set that information out in the same order as the template?
      `it was supplied electronically` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it supplied in electronic form?
      `it is a PDF or HTML file` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If electronic, is it a PDF or HTML file?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my consumer medicine information document meet the requirements` IF
        `it is in English`
    AND `it is clearly legible`
    AND `it is easily understood by patients`
    AND `it is consistent with the product information`
    AND `it sets out everything the TGA template requires`
    AND (    `it came in or on the pack`
         OR (    `it follows the template's order`
             AND (    (NOT `it was supplied electronically`)
                  OR `it is a PDF or HTML file`)))

-- reg 9B(1): a sponsor of goods (other than medical devices) commits an offence (10 penalty units) if "(a) the sponsor
-- supplies the goods on or after 1 July 2004; and (b) the sponsor knows the goods were manufactured using a human embryo
-- or human embryonic stem cell, or other material sourced from" one; "(c) the goods are of a kind specified in Part 1 of
-- Schedule 10; and (d) on or after 1 July 2004, the goods are included in the part of the Register for ... registered
-- goods or ... provisionally registered goods; and (e) the goods are supplied without written information stating" so.
-- (3): the statement goes in the consumer medicine information and in the product information. TRUE means the sponsor
-- must state it; the question does not ask whether it did.
@export Must I be told that my medicine was made using a human embryo or human embryonic stem cells (reg 9B)?
GIVEN `it is a medical device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the product a medical device rather than a medicine or biological?
      `the day it was supplied` IS A DATE @desc The day the sponsor supplied it, ISO 8601
      `the sponsor knows it was made using embryo material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the sponsor know it was made using a human embryo, human embryonic stem cell, or other material from one?
      `it contains or qualifies for a Poisons Standard Schedule 4, 8 or 9 substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain a Poisons Standard Schedule 4, 8 or 9 substance, or one that meets the criteria for those Schedules?
      `it is in Part 2 or 3 of Schedule 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a complementary or other non-prescription good the TGA accepted does not meet the criteria for Schedules 4, 8 or 9? Answer no if unsure.
      `it is one of the goods in items 2 to 15` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a medical gas, vaccine, allergen, biotechnology medicine, immunoglobulin, radio contrast agent, radiopharmaceutical, dialysis solution, special dosage form, injectable, blood product, or prescription medicine referred for evaluation?
      `it is registered or provisionally registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in the registered (AUST R) or provisionally registered part of the Register?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be told my medicine was made using human embryos` IF
        (NOT `it is a medical device`)
    AND `is on or after` `the day it was supplied` (`the date` 1 7 2004)
    AND `the sponsor knows it was made using embryo material`
    AND `is in Part 1 of Schedule 10` `it contains or qualifies for a Poisons Standard Schedule 4, 8 or 9 substance` `it is in Part 2 or 3 of Schedule 10` `it is one of the goods in items 2 to 15`
    AND `it is registered or provisionally registered`

§ `An unapproved medicine because my life was at risk` -- reg 12A; arises only if you were given a medicine or biological not on the Register because you were seriously ill

DECLARE `Medicine or biological` IS ONE OF
    `a medicine`
    `a biological`

DECLARE `Life-threatening exemption answer` IS ONE OF
    `the exemption covers it`
    `not covered: Poisons Standard Schedule 9 and 10 medicines are excluded`
    `not covered: nicotine pouches are excluded`
    `not covered: you are not a Category A patient`
    `not covered: you or your guardian did not give informed consent`
    `not covered: the practitioner's statement about you was not completed`
    `not covered: it was not dispensed on a prescription given in accordance with good medical practice`

@export Am I a Category A patient, so that an unapproved medicine can be given to me (reg 12A(5))?
GIVEN `I am seriously ill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you seriously ill? (a clinical judgment)
      `death is reasonably likely within a matter of months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is death from your condition reasonably likely within a matter of months?
      `premature death is reasonably likely without early treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is premature death from your condition reasonably likely without early treatment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a Category A patient` IF
    `is a Category A patient` `I am seriously ill` `death is reasonably likely within a matter of months` `premature death is reasonably likely without early treatment`

@export Was the consent I gave informed consent as the regulations define it (reg 12A(5))?
GIVEN `consent was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (or your guardian) consent to the treatment?
      `it was freely given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the consent freely given?
      `I was told the potential risks and benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given on the basis of information about the treatment's potential risks and benefits?
      `what I was told was enough to make an informed decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that information enough to let you make an informed decision whether to consent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my consent informed consent` IF
    `is informed consent` `consent was given` `it was freely given` `I was told the potential risks and benefits` `what I was told was enough to make an informed decision`

-- reg 12A(1): "all medicines are exempted from the operation of Part 3-2 of the Act (except section 31A and sections 31C
-- to 31F), other than ... (a) medicines of a class or kind listed in Schedule 9 or 10 to the Poisons Standard; (b)
-- nicotine pouches". (1A): all biologicals are exempt from Division 4 of Part 3-2A (no exclusions). (2): the exemption
-- "is subject to compliance with the following conditions: (a) the medicine or biological is to be given to a person who
-- satisfies the following criteria: (i) the person is a Category A patient ...; and (ii) the person, or the guardian of
-- the person, has given informed consent ...; and (iii) a statement in relation to the person, in the form approved by
-- the Secretary ..., is completed by the medical practitioner by whom, or at whose direction, the medicine or biological
-- is given to the person or by a health practitioner acting on behalf of that medical practitioner; and (b) the medicine
-- or biological is dispensed on the prescription of a medical practitioner who has prescribed the medicine or biological
-- in accordance with good medical practice." The first condition not met is reported, in the order of the text.
@export Could I lawfully be given a medicine or biological that is not on the Register because my life was at risk (reg 12A)?
GIVEN `what it is` IS A `Medicine or biological` @desc Was it a medicine, or a biological (a product made from human or animal cells or tissues)? One of: "a medicine", "a biological"
      `it is in Poisons Standard Schedule 9 or 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a medicine of a kind listed in Schedule 9 (prohibited substance) or Schedule 10 of the Poisons Standard?
      `it is a nicotine pouch` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a nicotine pouch?
      `I am seriously ill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you seriously ill? (a clinical judgment)
      `death is reasonably likely within a matter of months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was death from your condition reasonably likely within a matter of months?
      `premature death is reasonably likely without early treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was premature death reasonably likely without early treatment?
      `consent was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, or your guardian, consent to being given it?
      `it was freely given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the consent freely given?
      `I was told the potential risks and benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given on the basis of information about the potential risks and benefits?
      `what I was told was enough to make an informed decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that information enough to make an informed decision?
      `the statement about me was completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the doctor who gave or directed it (or a health practitioner for them) complete the TGA's approved statement (the SAS Category A form) about you?
      `it was dispensed on a medical practitioner's prescription` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it dispensed on a doctor's prescription?
      `it was prescribed in accordance with good medical practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it prescribed in accordance with good medical practice? (a judgment)
GIVETH A `Life-threatening exemption answer`
DECIDE `Could I lawfully be given an unapproved medicine because my life was at risk` IS
    BRANCH IF `what it is` EQUALS `a medicine` AND `it is in Poisons Standard Schedule 9 or 10`
           THEN `not covered: Poisons Standard Schedule 9 and 10 medicines are excluded`
           IF `what it is` EQUALS `a medicine` AND `it is a nicotine pouch`
           THEN `not covered: nicotine pouches are excluded`
           IF NOT (`is a Category A patient` `I am seriously ill` `death is reasonably likely within a matter of months` `premature death is reasonably likely without early treatment`)
           THEN `not covered: you are not a Category A patient`
           IF NOT (`is informed consent` `consent was given` `it was freely given` `I was told the potential risks and benefits` `what I was told was enough to make an informed decision`)
           THEN `not covered: you or your guardian did not give informed consent`
           IF NOT (`the statement about me was completed`)
           THEN `not covered: the practitioner's statement about you was not completed`
           IF NOT (`it was dispensed on a medical practitioner's prescription` AND `it was prescribed in accordance with good medical practice`)
           THEN `not covered: it was not dispensed on a prescription given in accordance with good medical practice`
           OTHERWISE `the exemption covers it`

-- reg 12A(3): the copy must reach the Secretary "within 28 days after the medicine or biological is given". A copy sent
-- on or before the day it was given is taken as sent in time (fork register).
@export Was the statement about me sent to the regulator within 28 days after I was given the unapproved medicine (reg 12A(3))?
GIVEN `a statement was completed about me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a practitioner complete the reg 12A statement (SAS Category A form) about you?
      `the day I was given it` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the medicine or biological, ISO 8601
      `a copy has been sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the statement been sent to the TGA?
      `the day the copy was sent` IS A DATE @desc If it has, the day it was sent, ISO 8601 (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Done in time or not`
DECIDE `Was the statement about me sent in time` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`a statement was completed about me`)
           THEN `there is no such duty on these facts`
           IF `a copy has been sent` AND (NOT (`is before` `the day I was given it` `the day the copy was sent`))
           THEN `done in time`
           OTHERWISE `the outcome of` (`reg 12A(3) -- the person who completed the statement must send a copy to the Secretary within 28 days after the medicine is given` (`day number of` (`the last day of` 28 `days after` `the day I was given it`) MINUS `day number of` `the day I was given it`)) `the day I was given it` `a copy has been sent` `the day the copy was sent` `today` (`the last day of` 28 `days after` `the day I was given it`)

§ `A medicine from an authorised prescriber or a health practitioner under the Minister's rules` -- regs 12B, 12BA, 12BB, 12C; arises only if a practitioner supplied you goods not on the Register under an authority or rules

DECLARE `Goods for an authority` IS ONE OF
    `a medicine (other than nicotine pouches)`
    `nicotine pouches`
    `a therapeutic vaping substance that is not a medicine`
    `a biological`

-- Act s 19(6) (s 32CM(4), (5) for biologicals): an authorised prescriber's authority "may only be given (a) to a medical
-- practitioner included in a class ... prescribed ...; and ... (b) in relation to a class or classes of recipients
-- prescribed". reg 12B(1), 12BA(1), 12C(1): the class is "medical practitioners engaged in clinical practice in or
-- outside a hospital". Recipients: reg 12B(2) (medicines), "persons each of whom is suffering from a life-threatening, or
-- otherwise serious, illness or condition"; reg 12C(3) (biologicals), "a life-threatening, or serious, illness or
-- condition"; reg 12BA(3) (vaping substances that are not medicines), "persons each of whom is seeking treatment for
-- smoking cessation or the management of nicotine dependence". reg 12BB(2): no approval or authority may be given for
-- nicotine pouches. TRUE means the Regulations let an authority reach you; whether your doctor's authority does depends
-- on its terms.
@export Can an authorised prescriber's authority cover my treatment (regs 12B, 12BA, 12BB, 12C)?
GIVEN `what it is` IS A `Goods for an authority` @desc What were you supplied? One of: "a medicine (other than nicotine pouches)", "nicotine pouches", "a therapeutic vaping substance that is not a medicine", "a biological"
      `my doctor is a medical practitioner in clinical practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prescriber a medical practitioner engaged in clinical practice (in or outside a hospital)?
      `my illness is life-threatening or serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you suffering from a life-threatening, or otherwise serious, illness or condition? (a judgment)
      `I am seeking treatment to stop smoking or manage nicotine dependence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you seeking treatment for smoking cessation or the management of nicotine dependence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an authorised prescriber's authority cover my treatment` IS
    CONSIDER `what it is`
    WHEN `nicotine pouches` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a therapeutic vaping substance that is not a medicine` THEN `my doctor is a medical practitioner in clinical practice` AND `I am seeking treatment to stop smoking or manage nicotine dependence`
    OTHERWISE `my doctor is a medical practitioner in clinical practice` AND `my illness is life-threatening or serious`

DECLARE `Ethics committee answer` IS ONE OF
    `an ethics committee's approval was needed`
    `no ethics committee approval was needed`
    `no authority can be given for nicotine pouches`

-- Act s 19(6)(aa) (s 32CM(4)(b) for biologicals): an authority may only be given to a practitioner "who has the approval
-- of an ethics committee", except in prescribed circumstances. Those are: reg 12B(1A) and 12C(2), a practitioner "engaged
-- in clinical practice outside a hospital" who "(a) has demonstrated that ... [they do] not have access to an ethics
-- committee that could approve the supply; and (b) has received an endorsement, from a specialist college with
-- established expertise relevant to the use"; reg 12B(1B), (1C), the supply to a patient of that practitioner of a
-- medicine matching an item in the tables (asked as one fact); reg 12BA(2), an authorised vaping substance "to be
-- administered by inhalation" for "the treatment of smoking cessation or management of nicotine dependence".
@export Did my doctor need an ethics committee's approval to be authorised to supply this to me (regs 12B, 12BA, 12C)?
GIVEN `what it is` IS A `Goods for an authority` @desc What were you supplied? One of: "a medicine (other than nicotine pouches)", "nicotine pouches", "a therapeutic vaping substance that is not a medicine", "a biological"
      `my doctor practises outside a hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the doctor practise outside a hospital?
      `my doctor showed there was no ethics committee they could use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the doctor demonstrated that they have no access to an ethics committee that could approve the supply?
      `my doctor has a specialist college endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the doctor received an endorsement to supply it from a specialist college with relevant expertise?
      `it matches an item in the reg 12B(1B) or (1C) tables` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a medicine: do its active ingredient (and strength), dosage form, route and indication match an item in the tables in reg 12B(1B) or (1C)? Your doctor can tell you.
      `it is inhaled to stop smoking or manage nicotine dependence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a vaping substance: is it inhaled, for smoking cessation or managing nicotine dependence?
GIVETH A `Ethics committee answer`
DECIDE `Did my doctor need an ethics committee's approval` IS
    CONSIDER `what it is`
    WHEN `nicotine pouches` THEN `no authority can be given for nicotine pouches`
    WHEN `a therapeutic vaping substance that is not a medicine` THEN
        IF `it is inhaled to stop smoking or manage nicotine dependence`
        THEN `no ethics committee approval was needed`
        ELSE `an ethics committee's approval was needed`
    WHEN `a biological` THEN
        IF `my doctor practises outside a hospital` AND `my doctor showed there was no ethics committee they could use` AND `my doctor has a specialist college endorsement`
        THEN `no ethics committee approval was needed`
        ELSE `an ethics committee's approval was needed`
    OTHERWISE
        IF    (`my doctor practises outside a hospital` AND `my doctor showed there was no ethics committee they could use` AND `my doctor has a specialist college endorsement`)
           OR `it matches an item in the reg 12B(1B) or (1C) tables`
        THEN `no ethics committee approval was needed`
        ELSE `an ethics committee's approval was needed`

-- reg 12B(5): rules made by the Minister under s 19(7A) of the Act "must not specify a medicine or a class of medicines
-- if the medicine ... contains a substance of a kind covered by an entry in Schedule 8, 9 or 10 to the Poisons
-- Standard". A flat negative: JUST FALSE. Otherwise it depends on the rules, which are not deposited: NOTHING.
@export Can a health practitioner supply me this medicine under the Minister's rules (reg 12B(5))?
GIVEN `it contains a Poisons Standard Schedule 8, 9 or 10 substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the medicine contain a substance in Schedule 8 (controlled drug), 9 or 10 of the Poisons Standard?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a health practitioner supply me this medicine under the Minister's rules` IS
    IF `it contains a Poisons Standard Schedule 8, 9 or 10 substance`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 12B(6) (medicines) and 12C(5) (biologicals): what a notification to the Secretary of a supply under the Minister's
-- rules (Act s 19(7C), s 32CM(7C)) "must" contain. The items about the patient and the goods are listed.
@export What information about me goes to the regulator when a practitioner notifies a supply to me under the Minister's rules (regs 12B(6), 12C(5))?
GIVEN `what it is` IS A `Medicine or biological` @desc Was it a medicine or a biological? One of: "a medicine", "a biological"
      `the release mechanism was clinically relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a medicine: was its release mechanism (for example slow release) clinically relevant to the supply?
      `the route was clinically relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a medicine: was its route of administration clinically relevant to the supply?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `What information about me goes to the regulator` IS
    CONSIDER `what it is`
    WHEN `a biological` THEN
        LIST "your initials, date of birth and gender",
             "each medical condition it was supplied for",
             "each indication it was supplied for",
             "the product name",
             "each active ingredient",
             "the route of administration",
             "the practitioner's name, AHPRA number and contact details",
             "the practitioner's health profession",
             "the address of the practitioner's principal place of practice"
    OTHERWISE
        concat (LIST (LIST "your initials, date of birth and gender",
                           "each medical condition it was supplied for",
                           "each indication it was supplied for",
                           "each active ingredient",
                           "the dosage form"),
                     (IF `the release mechanism was clinically relevant` THEN LIST "the release mechanism" ELSE EMPTY),
                     (IF `the route was clinically relevant` THEN LIST "the route of administration" ELSE EMPTY),
                     (LIST "the practitioner's name, AHPRA number and contact details",
                           "the practitioner's health profession",
                           "the address of the practitioner's principal place of practice"))

§ `A medicine I imported, or that was compounded for me` -- reg 12 and Schedule 5 items 1 and 6

DECLARE `Kind of goods` IS ONE OF
    `a medicine`
    `a biological`
    `other therapeutic goods`

DECLARE `Personal import answer` IS ONE OF
    `exempt under item 1 of Schedule 5`
    `not exempt: it is not for you or your immediate family`
    `not exempt: it contains a substance whose import the Customs Act prohibits`
    `not exempt: vaping goods and nicotine pouches are excluded`
    `not exempt: a biological needs a section 32CK approval`
    `not exempt: more than 3 months' supply in one importation`
    `not exempt: more than 15 months' supply in 12 months`
    `not exempt: the packaging does not let it be accurately identified`
    `not exempt: a Schedule 4 or 8 medicine needs a doctor's written authority`

-- reg 12(1) and Schedule 5 item 1: exempt are "therapeutic goods that are imported for therapeutic use in the treatment
-- of the importer or the importer's immediate family where: (a) the goods do not contain a substance the importation of
-- which is prohibited under the Customs Act 1901; and (b) the goods are not any of [the vaping goods] ... (vi) nicotine
-- pouches; and (ba) for a biological—the biological is the subject of an approval under section 32CK of the Act; and (c)
-- in the case of other medicines: (i) the quantity imported in one importation is not more than 3 months' supply at the
-- maximum dose recommended by the manufacturer; and (ii) the total quantity ... in the period of 12 months ending on the
-- day on which the latest importation occurs does not exceed 15 months' supply ...; and (iii) the medicine is in
-- packaging that enables the medicine to be accurately identified; or the medicines have been approved ... under
-- regulation 5 of the Customs (Prohibited Imports) Regulations 1956 ...; and (d) in the case of goods that are subject
-- to Schedule 4 or Schedule 8 to the current Poisons Standard—the goods are the subject of a written authority issued by
-- ... (i) if the goods are carried by the importer as a passenger on a ship or an aeroplane—a medical practitioner, or an
-- overseas medical practitioner treating the importer or the importer's immediate family; (ii) otherwise—a medical
-- practitioner". The first condition not met is reported, in the order of the text. Supply is counted in months at the
-- manufacturer's maximum recommended dose, as the person works it out.
@export Can I import this medicine for my own or my family's treatment without it being on the Register (Schedule 5 item 1)?
GIVEN `whose treatment it is for` IS A `Whose treatment` @desc Whose treatment is it for? One of: "my own", "my spouse or de facto partner", "my child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling", "a child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling of my spouse or de facto partner", "someone else"
      `what it is` IS A `Kind of goods` @desc Is it a medicine, a biological, or other therapeutic goods (not a medical device)? One of: "a medicine", "a biological", "other therapeutic goods"
      `it contains a substance the Customs Act bars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain a substance whose importation is prohibited under the Customs Act 1901?
      `it is a vaping good or nicotine pouch` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a vape, vaping liquid, vaping accessory, vaping kit or pack, or nicotine pouches?
      `the biological has a section 32CK approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a biological: is it the subject of a TGA approval under s 32CK of the Act?
      `months of supply in this importation` IS A NUMBER @desc For a medicine: how many months' supply this importation is, at the maximum dose the manufacturer recommends
      `months of supply imported in the 12 months to today` IS A NUMBER @desc For a medicine: the total months' supply imported for you or your family in the 12 months ending on the day of this importation, this one included
      `the packaging identifies it accurately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a medicine: is it in packaging that lets it be accurately identified?
      `it is approved under the Customs (Prohibited Imports) Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a medicine: has it (or its class) been approved for importation under reg 5 of the Customs (Prohibited Imports) Regulations 1956?
      `it is a Schedule 4 or 8 poison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a prescription-only (Schedule 4) or controlled (Schedule 8) substance under the Poisons Standard?
      `I carried it as a ship or aeroplane passenger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you bring it with you as a passenger on a ship or plane (rather than by post or courier)?
      `an Australian doctor gave written authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a written authority (a prescription or letter) for it from a doctor registered in Australia?
      `a treating overseas doctor gave written authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a written authority from an overseas doctor treating you or your family member?
GIVETH A `Personal import answer`
DECIDE `Can I import this medicine for my own treatment` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`is for me or my immediate family` `whose treatment it is for`)
           THEN `not exempt: it is not for you or your immediate family`
           IF `it contains a substance the Customs Act bars`
           THEN `not exempt: it contains a substance whose import the Customs Act prohibits`
           IF `it is a vaping good or nicotine pouch`
           THEN `not exempt: vaping goods and nicotine pouches are excluded`
           IF `what it is` EQUALS `a biological` AND (NOT `the biological has a section 32CK approval`)
           THEN `not exempt: a biological needs a section 32CK approval`
           IF `what it is` EQUALS `a medicine` AND (NOT `it is approved under the Customs (Prohibited Imports) Regulations`) AND `months of supply in this importation` GREATER THAN 3
           THEN `not exempt: more than 3 months' supply in one importation`
           IF `what it is` EQUALS `a medicine` AND (NOT `it is approved under the Customs (Prohibited Imports) Regulations`) AND `months of supply imported in the 12 months to today` GREATER THAN 15
           THEN `not exempt: more than 15 months' supply in 12 months`
           IF `what it is` EQUALS `a medicine` AND (NOT `it is approved under the Customs (Prohibited Imports) Regulations`) AND (NOT `the packaging identifies it accurately`)
           THEN `not exempt: the packaging does not let it be accurately identified`
           IF `it is a Schedule 4 or 8 poison` AND (NOT (`an Australian doctor gave written authority` OR (`I carried it as a ship or aeroplane passenger` AND `a treating overseas doctor gave written authority`)))
           THEN `not exempt: a Schedule 4 or 8 medicine needs a doctor's written authority`
           OTHERWISE `exempt under item 1 of Schedule 5`

DECLARE `Compounded answer` IS ONE OF
    `exempt under item 6 of Schedule 5`
    `not exempt: it was not dispensed or compounded for you`
    `not exempt: gene therapy medicines are excluded`
    `not exempt: medicinal cannabis products are excluded`
    `not exempt: GLP-1 receptor agonist analogues are excluded`
    `not exempt: nicotine pouches are excluded`

-- reg 12(1) and Schedule 5 item 6: exempt are "medicines that are dispensed, or extemporaneously compounded, for a
-- particular person for therapeutic application to that person, other than the following: (a) medicines that are used
-- for gene therapy; (b) medicines that are medicinal cannabis products; (c) medicines that contain glucagon-like
-- peptide-1 (GLP-1) receptor agonist analogues; (d) nicotine pouches". reg 2: "medicinal cannabis products means
-- therapeutic goods that contain, or are manufactured from, any part of a plant of the genus Cannabis".
@export Is a medicine dispensed or compounded for me exempt from being on the Register (Schedule 5 item 6)?
GIVEN `it was dispensed or compounded for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the medicine dispensed, or made up by a pharmacist (compounded), for you in particular, for your own treatment?
      `it is used for gene therapy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a medicine used for gene therapy?
      `it contains or is made from cannabis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain, or is it made from, any part of a cannabis plant?
      `it contains a GLP-1 receptor agonist analogue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain a GLP-1 receptor agonist analogue (for example semaglutide or tirzepatide)?
      `it is a nicotine pouch` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a nicotine pouch?
GIVETH A `Compounded answer`
DECIDE `Is a medicine compounded for me exempt` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`it was dispensed or compounded for me`)
           THEN `not exempt: it was not dispensed or compounded for you`
           IF `it is used for gene therapy`
           THEN `not exempt: gene therapy medicines are excluded`
           IF `it contains or is made from cannabis`
           THEN `not exempt: medicinal cannabis products are excluded`
           IF `it contains a GLP-1 receptor agonist analogue`
           THEN `not exempt: GLP-1 receptor agonist analogues are excluded`
           IF `it is a nicotine pouch`
           THEN `not exempt: nicotine pouches are excluded`
           OTHERWISE `exempt under item 6 of Schedule 5`

§ `A clinical trial I took part in` -- regs 12AB, 12AD and Schedule 5A item 3; arises only if you were given goods in a clinical trial

DECLARE `Trial route` IS ONE OF
    `an approval under section 19(1)(b) or 32CK of the Act`
    `a notification under item 3 of Schedule 5A`
    `neither`

DECLARE `Trial answer` IS ONE OF
    `within the conditions on these facts`
    `the regulations set no trial conditions on these facts`
    `outside: the trial was not notified before the goods were first used`
    `outside: the written good clinical practice assurance was not given before the trial started`
    `outside: the trial was not approved on terms at least as strict as the ethics committee advised`
    `outside: the Secretary found it contrary to the public interest and directed it to stop`
    `outside: the ethics committee advised against continuing the trial`
    `outside: an unproven Class 4 biological cannot be trialled under a notification`
    `outside: the use did not follow the Good Clinical Practice guideline`
    `outside: the use did not follow the protocol the ethics committee approved`
    `outside: the use did not follow the National Statement`
    `outside: the use went on after the ethics committee said it was inconsistent`

-- reg 12AD: "(a) the use of therapeutic goods in a clinical trial must be in accordance with the Practice Guideline; (b)
-- the use must comply with a procedural protocol approved by the ethics committee ...; (c) the use must be in accordance
-- with the ethical standards set out in the National Statement on Ethical Conduct in Research Involving Humans ...; (d)
-- the use must cease if the ethics committee ... informs the principal investigator that the use is inconsistent with"
-- the protocol or a condition of the approval.
-- reg 12AB(2), for an approval under s 19(1)(b) or 32CK: "Before any clinical trials ... are started, the Secretary,
-- must receive from the person to whom the approval is granted, and the principal investigator for each trial site: (a)
-- a written assurance that clinical trials will be conducted in accordance with the Guideline for Good Clinical Practice
-- ...; and (b) a written undertaking" to give information and allow inspection.
-- Schedule 5A item 3 (the notification route): (a) the sponsor must notify the Secretary before "the goods begin to be
-- used in the trial" (or by an agreed later time); (c), (d) the goods must be approved by the sponsor or trial body
-- "having regard to the advice of the ethics committee", on terms "no less restrictive than the terms advised by the
-- ethics committee"; (e) "the Secretary must not, at any time: (i) have become aware that to conduct or continue the
-- trial would be contrary to the public interest; and (ii) have directed that the trial not be conducted, or be
-- stopped"; (f) the sponsor or trial body "must not receive, or have received, advice from the ethics committee that is
-- inconsistent with the continuation of the trial"; (g) reg 12AD applies; (h) the goods are not a Class 4 biological
-- without clinical trial approval for an equivalent indication from a comparable regulator, or without a history of
-- previous use supported by clinical evidence. The fees, site notifications and the sponsor's duties to an authorised
-- officer ((b), (ha), (hb), (i)-(k)) are out (NOTES.md). The first condition not met is reported.
@export Was the clinical trial I took part in run within the conditions the regulations set (regs 12AB, 12AD, Schedule 5A item 3)?
GIVEN `the trial route` IS A `Trial route` @desc How was the trial authorised? One of: "an approval under section 19(1)(b) or 32CK of the Act" (a CTA), "a notification under item 3 of Schedule 5A" (a CTN), "neither"
      `it was notified before the goods were first used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a notified trial: did the sponsor notify the TGA before the goods began to be used in the trial (or by a later time the TGA agreed)?
      `the assurance was given before the trial started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an approved trial: did the approval holder and each principal investigator give the TGA the written good clinical practice assurance and undertaking before the trial started?
      `it was approved on the ethics committee's advice and terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a notified trial: did the sponsor or trial body approve the goods' use having regard to the ethics committee's advice, on terms no less strict than the committee advised?
      `the Secretary found it against the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the TGA become aware that running or continuing the trial would be contrary to the public interest?
      `the Secretary directed it to stop` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the TGA directed that the trial not be run, or be stopped?
      `the ethics committee advised against continuing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a notified trial: did the sponsor or trial body receive advice from the ethics committee inconsistent with continuing the trial?
      `it is a Class 4 biological` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the goods a Class 4 biological (for example a cell or gene therapy product)?
      `a comparable regulator approved a trial for the same indication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a Class 4 biological: has a regulator with comparable requirements approved a clinical trial for an equivalent indication?
      `it has a history of use backed by clinical evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a Class 4 biological: does it have a history of previous use supported by clinical evidence given to the TGA?
      `the use followed the GCP guideline` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the use of the goods on you in accordance with the ICH Guideline for Good Clinical Practice? (a judgment)
      `the use followed the approved protocol` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the use comply with the protocol the ethics committee approved?
      `the use followed the National Statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the use in accordance with the NHMRC National Statement on Ethical Conduct in Research Involving Humans? (a judgment)
      `the committee told the investigator the use was inconsistent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the ethics committee tell the principal investigator the use was inconsistent with the protocol or the approval's conditions?
      `the use went on after that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did the use of the goods go on after that?
GIVETH A `Trial answer`
DECIDE `Was my clinical trial run within the conditions` IS
    BRANCH IF `the trial route` EQUALS `neither`
           THEN `the regulations set no trial conditions on these facts`
           IF `the trial route` EQUALS `a notification under item 3 of Schedule 5A` AND (NOT `it was notified before the goods were first used`)
           THEN `outside: the trial was not notified before the goods were first used`
           IF `the trial route` EQUALS `an approval under section 19(1)(b) or 32CK of the Act` AND (NOT `the assurance was given before the trial started`)
           THEN `outside: the written good clinical practice assurance was not given before the trial started`
           IF `the trial route` EQUALS `a notification under item 3 of Schedule 5A` AND (NOT `it was approved on the ethics committee's advice and terms`)
           THEN `outside: the trial was not approved on terms at least as strict as the ethics committee advised`
           IF `the trial route` EQUALS `a notification under item 3 of Schedule 5A` AND `the Secretary found it against the public interest` AND `the Secretary directed it to stop`
           THEN `outside: the Secretary found it contrary to the public interest and directed it to stop`
           IF `the trial route` EQUALS `a notification under item 3 of Schedule 5A` AND `the ethics committee advised against continuing`
           THEN `outside: the ethics committee advised against continuing the trial`
           IF `the trial route` EQUALS `a notification under item 3 of Schedule 5A` AND `it is a Class 4 biological` AND ((NOT `a comparable regulator approved a trial for the same indication`) OR (NOT `it has a history of use backed by clinical evidence`))
           THEN `outside: an unproven Class 4 biological cannot be trialled under a notification`
           IF NOT (`the use followed the GCP guideline`)
           THEN `outside: the use did not follow the Good Clinical Practice guideline`
           IF NOT (`the use followed the approved protocol`)
           THEN `outside: the use did not follow the protocol the ethics committee approved`
           IF NOT (`the use followed the National Statement`)
           THEN `outside: the use did not follow the National Statement`
           IF `the committee told the investigator the use was inconsistent` AND `the use went on after that`
           THEN `outside: the use went on after the ethics committee said it was inconsistent`
           OTHERWISE `within the conditions on these facts`
